==============================================================================
PART C -- 4-monomial sample: does the bound scale the same way?
==============================================================================
  sampled 40 two-sided 4-monomial patterns (deg <= 3): ALL closed = True; max M* = 8
  M* <= charge span + 1 on the sample?  False

SUMMARY
  DECIDABILITY (rigorous): GMC(2) on {<= k monomials, degree <= D} is a FINITE union of
  Groebner tests -- so it is DECIDABLE, and every trinomial pattern up to degree 4
  (and a 4-monomial sample) CLOSES. That is UNCONDITIONAL GMC(2) on those bounded
  families -- no conjecture used, only Hilbert's Nullstellensatz + finite computation.
  MOMENT BOUND: M* stays small and tracks the charge span; the fitted bound is the
  data for HYP-8535, which (if proved uniform) upgrades this to full GMC(2).
